<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Radar&amp;nbsp;Multi-Target Echo&amp;nbsp;Signals&amp;nbsp;under Multi-PRI&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Simulation Task&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;This example shows how to generate a Radar Receiver test signal using sequencer and play them out in M8190A or M9381A.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Required Softwares&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Make sure you have installed Keysight IO Library Version 15 (or up) and Keysight Connection Expert softwares. SystemVue 2013.01 (or up) product.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Workspace Description&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;1. Run the equation &apos;Generate Signals&apos; by clicking &apos;GO&apos; to generate three multi-target radar echo signals under multi-PRI&amp;nbsp;at different carrier frequency of 2.3 GHz,&amp;nbsp;2.5 GHz, 2.7 GHz. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;2. Open the Waveform&amp;nbsp;Sequence Composer UI by click on the &quot;WaveformSeq1&quot; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;BLOCKQUOTE style=&quot;MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px&quot; dir=ltr&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;(1) Note under &quot;Pattern&quot; tab the sequence is composed from the waveform data at each corresponding dataset. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;(2) Go to &quot;Instrument&quot; tab. Type the IP address of the M8190 instrument into the &quot;Address&quot; cell of in the table under &quot;Instrument Selection&quot; area. As an alternative, you can click the &quot;Select Instrument...&quot; button to pick the instrument if it has been added into the &quot;Keysight Connection Expert&quot;, or add it in the &quot;Select Instruments&quot; dialog. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;(3) Adjust the instrument parameters if needed. Note that &quot;AutoScale&quot; parameter is set up to auto scale all waveforms. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BLOCKQUOTE&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;3. Click the &quot;Execute&quot; button and the waveforms should be downloaded into the M8190 and the sequence will be played out. &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;************************************************&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4 face=Calibri&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Further exploration&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 10pt&quot;&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;************************************************&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;Playing out of the sequence can also be emulated by using &quot;WaveformSequencer&quot; part in a schematic. For each schematic shown in this example, you can simply drag the &quot;Frequency Hopping Sequence&quot; icon on the workspace tree and drop it into the schematic and a &quot;WaveformSequencer&quot; part will be automatically placed into the schematic and properly configured.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face=Calibri&gt;If VSA 89600 software is available, then enable the two VSA_89600_Sink&apos;s. Now you are able to see the emulated signal &quot;live&quot; in VSA 89600 application.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;</Text>
